WEBVTT

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.750
"15 Years Ago Aomori Prefecture"

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.410
"15 Years Ago Aomori Prefecture"

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.410
Mary, did you...

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.080
Sorry!

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.620
Just this once, okay?

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.540
I love you, sis!

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.160
"12 Years Ago"

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.950
"12 Years Ago"

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.950
Another delicious meal!

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.540
Really? Hooray!

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:32.620
Sorry for always making you do the cooking.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.830
Nah, it's fine.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.950
You think Dad's not coming home ever again?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:45.370
You've got me, Mary!

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.120
Yeah!

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.250
Come on, let's go.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.080
You don't need to worry.

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.870
I don't want to leave her!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.450
I need to stay with my sis!

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:58.700
Sis! Sis!

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.750
Mary!

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.830
Let's leave town together!

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.250
Don't worry! I'll protect you, Mary!

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:11.000
Okay!

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:16.750
"Kabukicho 221st Avenue"

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.450
"Kabukicho 221st Avenue"

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.450
Kabukicho. Nobody will ever find us here.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.660
"Kabukicho 221st Avenue"

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:24.660
So we can be together, sis?

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.080
In the darkness of Kabukicho,
where elephants roar to sound the time,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.120
and villains lurk in every shadow,

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.700
you'll find six detectives.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.660
Weirdos, freaks, bozos and fools to a man,

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.330
"Sherlock Holmes"

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.330
Weirdos, freaks, bozos and fools to a man,

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:43.790
who knows what madness
they'll bring with them.

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.750
"Fuyuto Kyogoku"

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:44.750
who knows what madness
they'll bring with them.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:45.750
"Michel Belmont"

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:45.750
who knows what madness
they'll bring with them.

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.700
"Lucy Morstan"                         "Mary Morstan"

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:46.700
Just sit back and watch as they
compete to solve the riddle.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.370
"Torataro Kobayashi"

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:47.370
Just sit back and watch as they
compete to solve the riddle.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:51.330
Just sit back and watch as they
compete to solve the riddle.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.410
"Offside is the Best Side"

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.790
Wonderful!

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:33.330
Where would you wear something like this?

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:33.950
He's back!

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.830
"The Legendary Stud Farm Host!!"
"Masaya Comeback Event"

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.830
He's back!

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.080
"The Legendary Stud Farm Host!!"
"Masaya Comeback Event"

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.080
The legend is coming back!

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:43.160
You've all got to come! Aaah!

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:49.540
If I wear it there, the whole room
won't be able to take their eyes off me!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.540
Just imagining it makes me shiver.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.330
"Teawater Seminar"

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.330
Just imagining it makes me shiver.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:04.330
The Mrs. is rough on people sometimes.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.790
It's okay.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:11.200
Pipe here is in a good mood
now that they're all cleaned up.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:12.580
Is that...

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.410
We're sorry!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.500
You saved me!

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.660
Um, can I do something to thank you?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.000
Just be quiet.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.250
Thank you!

00:04:35.910 --> 00:04:38.580
Way to go, Lady Lu!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.120
Huh?

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:55.830
"Kuromi Team"

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:04.500
Um...

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.750
I'm a big fan!

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.910
I made this myself. If you'd be so kind...

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.040
So the Lady Lu's in love, huh?

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.910
And with a sumo wrestler?

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:24.250
I didn't know there was
a sumo team there, though.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.000
Oh, the Kuromi Team? Yeah?

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.160
Honestly, I don't hear
good things about them.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.370
"Kuromi Team Sekitori"

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.370
So his name's Omiyama.

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:39.580
Oh, I remember that name.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:43.700
He was said to be in line to be
a yokozuna when he was young.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:47.450
It was a long time ago.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.160
He hasn't been that great
since he broke his knee.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.000
In his last tournament, he barely even played.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:56.410
And he's not much today, huh?

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:58.660
He may not win many matches,

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:03.250
but the neighbors say he's the
only one of them with a good heart.

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.500
A good heart, huh?

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.410
If only he was a little smarter.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.250
Jeez... He's a boring man.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.040
If he loses this next tournament,
he's getting knocked down to <i>makushita</i> .

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:21.290
Given his age, he'll be thinking about retiring.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:25.540
That explains why Lady Lu
is cheering him on so much.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.580
It's hard to save much money.

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.870
"Teawater Seminar Information Pamphlet"

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.870
Sis, I want to go to a cram school!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.950
"Tuition    2,000,000 Yen Per Year
Entrance Fees          80,000 Yen
Electives                50,000 Yen"

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.870
You need 2,000,000 yen in two days?

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:46.080
I always wanted to be a
glamorous student, you know.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.580
But we don't have the money...

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.040
Yeah, that's right.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.540
Sorry. Forget that I said anything--

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.330
Don't worry.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.330
Sorry. Forget that I said anything--

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.040
I'll get the money.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:02.080
Really?

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:06.620
Yeah. Don't worry about a thing.
Just focus on studying.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:12.250
I know! I'll do the cleaning and
washing every day from now on!

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.830
Thanks!

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.000
And...

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.950
I'll take over cooking again--

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.830
Absolutely not.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:23.290
I'll do it, so stay out of the kitchen.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.910
Y-Yeah?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.540
"Kaneko Financing"

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:29.540
Fine, I'll lend you the money.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:30.790
Thank you, Boss Kaneko!

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.080
"Boss of Kaneko Financing"

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.080
Thank you, Boss Kaneko!

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.200
"Boss of Kaneko Financing"

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.200
But you've got two weeks to return the money.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:42.620
If you can't pay me back by then,
you'll have to work at one of my shops.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.830
Shops...

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.950
Understood!

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:54.620
I'll make sure to pay you back on time.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:07.700
It's rare to see Moriarty all the way out here.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.910
Lucy!

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.160
That's a lot of stuff you've got.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:18.660
Oh, it's summer vacation, so I'm
going to a friend's house to stay.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:22.080
He's just sitting up there...

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.910
I think he's about to jump. Don't you?

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.620
What's wrong with you? Let's stop him.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:29.200
Hey, stop!

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:32.620
Let me go!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.200
I can't let you jump!

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.410
Hey, help!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.910
Huh? Okay...

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:38.870
Pull!

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.410
Huh?

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:45.250
You're...

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:45.250
Just get off me!

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:46.700
"Coffee of Silence"

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.660
"Coffee of Silence"

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.660
Here.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.950
Thank you.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.950
Who's this? You know him?

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.660
No, not really...

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:57.950
I'm part of the Kuromi team. My name
is Bunmaru, and I'm Omiyama's attendant.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:02.700
"Rikishi, Omiyama's Attendant"

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:02.700
I'm part of the Kuromi team. My name
is Bunmaru, and I'm Omiyama's attendant.

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.500
So why are you up here?

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:10.750
Um, well, it all started when...

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:16.950
Our building is old and falling apart,
so we decided to repair it.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:20.870
Oh, that building, yeah. It's falling apart.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.700
And?

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:29.000
Last night, I was given 2,000,000 yen
from our supporters to repair it, but...

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.290
I got drunk and lost it!

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.500
Two million yen!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:37.040
Really? Well, guess you have to die then!

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.200
We need to pay the contractors by noon!

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.830
Let me take responsibility by killing myself!

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:45.040
Knock it off!

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:48.450
If you do that, you'll cause
trouble for Omiyama, too!

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:52.700
But I can't go back alive!

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.450
What is this money?

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.580
It's yours.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:01.200
I can't take it.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.700
Just take it.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.580
Thank you!

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.950
Now I've done it!

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.620
I'm sorry, Mary!

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:15.500
Mary?

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:19.290
She asked you for something
else again, didn't she?

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:22.700
Why do you always go along with
whatever selfish thing she asks you for?

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:28.410
Yeah, Mary causes a ton
of problems for me. But...

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.370
She's my only sister.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:38.250
You've got a sister, too, right?
So you understand.

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:39.830
I guess.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:43.580
So I have to make this work out somehow!

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:49.830
Here. Another 2,000,000.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:53.700
But I'm not extending your
deadline another second.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.580
You okay with that?

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.450
I'll make it work!

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:00.910
I'll make 4,000,000 yen in two weeks!

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.330
Crap. I overslept.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:15.160
Sis!

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:18.160
So you want some work, then?

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:22.660
I've got a lot of A Rank jobs
that are open to anybody.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.450
Really? Then...

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.000
Excuse me.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:30.450
I'm told that Lucy Morstan is here.

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.410
Thank you so much.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:36.330
No, it's fine...

00:11:36.330 --> 00:11:39.950
Thanks to you, we were able
to pay for the repairs.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.790
That's so great.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:45.330
But how'd you lose all that money?

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:51.000
Well, I got the 2,000,000 yen
at our supporter's office yesterday;

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:53.500
when I was there they
gave me something to drink.

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.540
I was worried from the start.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:02.120
He's a bad drinker and
passes out in the street often.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.660
That's right.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.000
So...

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.870
I tried to not drink too much,

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:13.410
but on the way back, I got really tired...

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:20.160
It's gone!

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:24.410
When I woke up, the money was gone!

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:27.410
It's gone!

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:31.160
And the rest, you know...

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:33.160
Did you talk to the cops?

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:40.450
No. I'm keeping it to myself
in order to protect Bunmaru's future.

00:12:40.450 --> 00:12:44.700
Of course, I'll return
the 2,000,000 when I can.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:50.000
My attendant's failures
are my responsibility, after all.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.950
You haven't changed...

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:57.830
Not at all. Don't worry about it.

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:59.250
Oh, right.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:04.250
The food you brought was delicious.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:07.790
Yeah? It's been a while since I've
been that confident in my cooking.

00:13:07.790 --> 00:13:10.870
It's amazing that you made it yourself.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.200
It was nice and chewy,
like you'd buy at a store--

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:16.120
Bunmaru, are you sure
you feel bad about this?

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:18.500
Sorry!

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.580
I think I know what's going on here.

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.830
Kuma, go buy some for me.

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:25.410
Sure. Buy what?

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:28.000
We'll be going, then.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:31.540
Oh, I'm cheering for you
in the next tournament!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.660
Please do your best!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.000
It's fine to cheer him on,

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.750
but don't you need to earn money?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.410
That's right!

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:48.080
I don't care how minor they are.
Give me every job you have right now!

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.080
Hello?

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:11.250
Is that...?

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:16.950
...1,970,000. 1,980,000. 1,990,000...

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.330
...2,000,000.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.200
"Reminder Payment Date - Today"

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:33.200
Hey, how've you been, doc?

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:37.120
Boss! You were so good
to me on the West Side.

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.660
It's thanks to you that I made it to Kabukicho.

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:42.870
You used to this place now?

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:44.040
Yes.

00:14:44.040 --> 00:14:47.290
Um... He hasn't heard
about my case yet, though.

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.580
I see.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:53.450
Well, you're dealing with
that <i>rakugo</i> -loving weirdo.

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:55.580
He's hopeless, that fool.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:15:00.040
He's making me work really hard, really.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:01.870
But...

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:05.500
It's hard to hate him.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:10.080
Well, he's good at his job, so hang in there.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.830
Okay, thank you!

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:19.450
Hey, how's Little Lu doing?

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:20.910
Let me go!

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:22.500
Just come with me!

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:22.500
Let me go!

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.870
Sherlock- <i>san</i> , you know the deal, right?

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:27.750
Lend her the money!
You've got more than enough!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.580
Leave me alone!

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:31.580
I can't!

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:34.120
You need to get another 2,000,000 yen today.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:36.790
Just get it back yourself.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:43.120
The one who stole the 2,000,000
from that stupid attendant...

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.950
...hasn't used it yet.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:48.120
You know who took it?

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:50.120
Of course.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.120
You want to hear?

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:53.120
Yes! Of course!

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.450
Hey, old man.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:07.290
They say you found out who
stole the money from Bunmaru?

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:13.250
Yeah. By the way, Kuma, you want one
of the <i>daifuku</i> I had you buy the other day?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.750
It's good, but...

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.830
What's the deal with that?

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:27.040
That's the snack Bunmaru ate.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.580
Omiyama!

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.910
I challenge you!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.500
Stop it! Get away from Mary!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:47.290
Get away from me!

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:48.700
Sis!

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:51.160
You're coming with us.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.660
What are you doing to that little girl?

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:59.790
We're sorry!

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:06.330
You were protecting your sister? That's good.

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:12.410
It's not easy to live in this town,
but stay on the straight and narrow.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.160
Got it!

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:16.830
Omiyama!

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.540
What are you doing?

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:25.330
Lucy- <i>san</i> , why are you doing this?

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:31.500
I always admired you!

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:35.500
The person on the straight and
narrow that I thought you were!

00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:40.540
I'll pass. They've got a sleeping drug in them.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:43.620
Sl-Sleeping drug?

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.870
It was a pain in the ass to get my hands on it.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:49.250
Kids these days are big into the stuff.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:52.290
I guess they like the fact
it takes a while to kick in.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:55.790
But what do you mean this is what he ate?

00:17:55.790 --> 00:17:58.700
Bunmaru ate what Lucy made, right?

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:03.500
You didn't know? Lucy's cooking was terrible.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:09.450
She's so bad that even a girl like
Mary's willing to do the cooking,

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.580
which means she must be terrible.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:12.870
Which means...

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:17.250
Bunmaru ate something else.

00:18:17.250 --> 00:18:21.540
But how'd you know it was
the <i>daifuku</i> that he ate?

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:26.330
Bunmaru didn't drink that much,
but he felt very tired.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:30.290
And the <i>daifuku</i> he ate was very chewy.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:35.000
So that's where I got the idea, and then
I showed them to Bunmaru himself.

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:39.370
So the criminal made Bunmaru pass out
with sleeping drug-filled <i>daifuku</i>

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.450
and then stole the money?

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:45.540
Was it Lucy?

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:48.290
You moron. Were you paying attention?

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:54.370
We were just saying that the criminal
swapped Lucy's present out for these.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:57.870
So who was it, really?

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.120
I'm sorry.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.580
Omiyama was the one who did it.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.910
I stole the money from Bunmaru.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:07.200
"Dear Omiyama" "I'm cheering you on!
